<http://example.org/sen0401/ch14/diagrams> a owl:Ontology ; rdfs:label "SEN0401 ch14 narrative diagrams - ABox"@en ; owl:versionInfo "1.0.0" ; dcterms:identifier "sen0401_ch14_diagrams_abox_v1_0_0" ;
    rdfs:comment "The chapter's authored diagrams as cme:NarrativeDiagram individuals: generated by sen0401_page_data_v2_11_0.py from sen0401_ch14_diagrams_v1_0_0.py, typed by the CME narrative-to-diagram mapping (a module of cme_standards_adoption_v1_3_0.ttl, CME 0.16.0)."@en ; owl:imports <http://example.org/cme/narrative-diagram> .

chx:Diagram_CheckSecondPayment a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "How a node treats a second payment of the same output"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Workflow ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:ActivityDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 14, A double spend is rejected: a second payment of the same output with a lower fee was refused as an insufficient replacement, one with a higher fee replaced the first in the memory pool" ; cme:elementCount 5 ;
    cme:accompanies "DoubleSpendRejected" ; rdfs:comment "the passage is a procedure with a decision - does the second payment carry a higher fee - and a different outcome on each branch: a workflow"@en .
chx:Diagram_SecondLayerInFiveBranches a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "Second-layer applications in five branches"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:TopicAndParts ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:MindMap ; cme:readFrom "chapter 14, the whole chapter: platform guarantees, colored coins, payment channels, the Lightning Network and what changed since the print" ; cme:elementCount 19 ;
    cme:accompanies "PlatformGuarantees" ; cme:accompanies "ColoredCoins" ; cme:accompanies "PaymentChannels" ; cme:accompanies "LightningNetwork" ; cme:accompanies "SinceThePrint" ; rdfs:comment "the chapter lays out one subject, second-layer applications, by its parts: a topic and its parts"@en .
chx:Diagram_HtlcExchange a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "A payer and a receiver use the secret branch of an HTLC"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Interaction ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:SequenceDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 14, The HTLC secret branch: the hash branch pays whoever shows the secret and the receiver's signature; a wrong secret was refused" ; cme:elementCount 4 ;
    cme:accompanies "HtlcSecretBranch" ; cme:accompanies "HtlcTimeoutBranch" ; rdfs:comment "the passage is an exchange between a payer and a receiver in an order that matters - the lock, then the secret and the signature: an interaction"@en .
chx:Diagram_RefundLadderLife a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "Six commitments with falling lock times, from refused to the sixth accepted"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:LifeCycle ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:StateDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 14, The refund timelock ladder: the six commitments had lock times from 488 down to 483, all were refused as non-final at the start, at height 483 only the sixth was accepted, and once it was mined the earlier ones were refused because their input was gone" ; cme:elementCount 5 ;
    cme:accompanies "RefundTimelockLadder" ; rdfs:comment "the passage describes the states the commitments are in and the events that move them - refused, the sixth accepted, the earlier ones refused: a life cycle"@en .
chx:Diagram_RouteRoles a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "What the sender and an intermediary each do in a routed payment"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:SetOfUses ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:UseCaseDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 14, The fee arithmetic: with a fee of 0.001 from each of three intermediaries the sender must offer 1.003, and the payment of 1 bitcoin cost 300,000 satoshis in fees" ; cme:elementCount 6 ;
    cme:accompanies "FeeArithmetic" ; cme:accompanies "TimelockStaircase" ; rdfs:comment "the passage lists what the different parties of a route do, under different conditions: a set of uses by actors"@en .
